{
  "manufacturer": "Carrier",
  "manufacturer_slug": "carrier",
  "model": "ComfortVu BACnet Thermostat",
  "model_slug": "comfortvu-thermostat",
  "aliases": [
    "ComfortVu",
    "Carrier ComfortVu",
    "11-808-726-01"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Networked room thermostat",
  "applies_to": "Carrier ComfortVu wall thermostats controlling fan coils or AC/heat pump units.",
  "summary": "The ComfortVu is a touchscreen room thermostat that can talk BACnet MS/TP on an RS-485 bus (a DIP switch selects BACnet or Modbus). Its object list mixes live values (temperatures, outputs, occupancy) with the technician settings, so many installer parameters are writable over the network. Several object instances are reused with different names depending on whether the thermostat is set up for a fan coil (FC) or an AC/heat pump (AC) system, so expect only one of each pair to exist on a given unit.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "notes": [
    "MS/TP baud rates 9600, 19200, 38400 or 76800, 8N1.",
    "DIP switch configuration (AC vs FC system) decides which objects exist; some instances appear twice in the list with an AC name and an FC name.",
    "Mode, fan speed and similar enumerations are Analog Values carrying integer codes, not Multistate objects.",
    "The device instance itself can be changed by writing AV42 (BacnetDeviceInstanceNumber).",
    "Many writable AVs mirror the thermostat's technician (P) settings."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "ComfortVu BACnet Thermostat Points List and Technician Settings",
